  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rajesh Patel vs State Of U.P. on 2 November, 2020 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 70 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 33880 of 2020 Applicant :- Rajesh Patel Opposite Party :- State of U.P.",
    "facts": "The instant bail application has been filed on behalf of the applicant, Rajesh Patel, with a prayer to release him on bail in Case Crime No. 108 of 2020 under Sections 272, 273 I.P.C. r/w Section 60 of Excise Act and Section 3 (1) of U.P. Gangsters and Anti-Social Activities (Prevention) Act, 1986, Police Station- Machhalishahar, District- Jaunpur, during pendency of trial. The allegation against the applicant in the F.I.R. is that he along with his gang was involved in sale, supply and theft of spurious liquor. The recovery of spurious liquor has been allegedly made from the co-accused. Regarding proceedings u/s U.P. Gangsters and Anti-Social Activities (Prevention) Act, 1986, there are 4 cases against the applicant including the present case.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant has submitted that the applicant has been implicated for offences u/s 272, 273 I.P.C. r/w Section 60 of Excise Act together. He has submitted that the offences u/s 272, 273 I.P.C. require to be investigated under the Food Safety and Standards Act and the complaint lies for prosecution of such offences. Offence u/s 60 of the Excise Act are triable by Magistrate. The applicant is in jail since 25.08.2020. Learned A.G.A. has opposed the prayer for bail of the applicant. Keeping in view the nature of the offence, argument advanced on behalf of the parties, spreading of novel corona virus in jails, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another, reported in (2018) 3 SCC 22 and without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case, let the applicant involved in the aforesaid crime be released on bail on his furnishing a personal bond and two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of the court concerned with the following conditions that :- 1.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant has submitted that the applicant has been implicated for offences u/s 272, 273 I.P.C. r/w Section 60 of Excise Act together. He has submitted that the offences u/s 272, 273 I.P.C. require to be investigated under the Food Safety and Standards Act and the complaint lies for prosecution of such offences. Offence u/s 60 of the Excise Act are triable by Magistrate. The applicant is in jail since 25.08.2020. Learned A.G.A. has opposed the prayer for bail of the applicant.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Keeping in view the nature of the offence, argument advanced on behalf of the parties, spreading of novel corona virus in jails, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another, reported in (2018) 3 SCC 22 and without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case, let the applicant involved in the aforesaid crime be released on bail on his furnishing a personal bond and two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of the court concerned with the following conditions that :- 1."
  },
